# keur quality control — a Go repo whose sonar-project.properties configures no
# coverage report path (Sonar then shows 0% coverage).
#
# Why this exists: for Go, Sonar reads coverage from a `go test -coverprofile`
# report via `sonar.go.coverage.reportPaths`. Miss it and coverage reads 0% and
# any coverage gate fails silently.
#
# HOW (requires + absence): `requires: lang: go` gates to repos containing Go
# (facts, ADR-009). The absence engine fires when the key appears NOWHERE.
# `content_contains: sonar.sources` skips files with no analysis.
#
# WARN, low confidence: coverage may be passed via CI or skipped on purpose.
# @see docs/rules-authoring.md
id: SONAR-008
ilities: [testability]
maturity: 3
title: Go repo — Sonar config has no coverage report path
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: absence
action: warn
confidence: 0.5
requires:
  lang: go
target:
  filenames: sonar-project.properties
  content_contains: sonar.sources
patterns:
  - regex: (?mi)^\s*sonar\.go\.coverage\.reportPaths\s*=\s*\S
    message: "Go repo: sonar-project.properties sets sonar.sources but no sonar.go.coverage.reportPaths — Sonar will show 0% coverage. Point it at your coverage profile."
fix: "Add `sonar.go.coverage.reportPaths=coverage.out` and generate it with `go test ./... -coverprofile=coverage.out` before the scan."
